WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.168
In this video, you'll get free test keys from FedEx, enter them in the plugin, and see how to prove they work.

00:00:06.618 --> 00:00:12.666
You need two things: your FedEx account number, and a free developer account on FedEx's developer portal.

00:00:13.116 --> 00:00:19.500
There, create a project and turn on the rates, ship, and tracking APIs. Stay in test mode.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:26.862
Copy the test account number, the API key, and the secret key. FedEx shows that secret only once.

00:00:27.312 --> 00:00:33.768
In your store's admin, open FedEx Shipping, then Settings. The keys go on three of the five tabs.

00:00:34.218 --> 00:00:40.962
On this demo store the credentials are already saved, so the Client Secret field shows dots instead of what you'd type.

00:00:41.412 --> 00:00:48.996
Tracking needs its own second key pair on the Tracking tab. Without it, tracking quietly stops — no error appears.

00:00:49.446 --> 00:00:55.950
On the Account tab, use the test account number from your project, and leave the Environment dropdown on Sandbox.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:04.104
One Save Changes button at the bottom saves all five tabs at once. Below it, the quota panel shows today's usage.

00:01:04.554 --> 00:01:11.274
There's no test connection button — real rates at checkout are the test. Next, add FedEx to a shipping zone.

